>Sounds reasonable.  As a counterweight, make alchemy less reliable.  
>Give even blessed and properly mixed potions a chance to explode, 

They already do have such a chance.  Any alchemy operation not
involving a potion of acid or a cursed potion has a 10% chance of
causing an alchemical blast; this is checked *before* any attempt to
determine what kind of potion would be produced by the operation.

(All alchemy operations involving acid or curses automatically explode.)

>and calculate damage per exploded bottle (all potions explode).  

That would be amusingly vicious, but I think it might be overkill.
